#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:159
msgid "State Update"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:161
msgid "The following interfaces are used to set entity states."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:0
msgid "`SetEntityState`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:0
msgid "`/gzserver/set_entity_state`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:0
msgid "Set the pose and twist of a specific entity"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:167
msgid "SetEntityState Service"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:169
msgid "Set the pose and twist of a specific entity."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:171
msgid ""
"ros2 service call /gzserver/set_entity_state simulation_interfaces/srv/"
"SetEntityState \"{ entity: 'my_model', state: {pose: { position: { x: -2.0, "
"z: 0.5 }}, twist: {linear: {x: 0.5}}}}\"\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:176
msgid ""
"When using `SetEntityState`, it is currently not possible to set just the "
"`pose` or the `twist` of an entity. Both components of the entity will be "
"assigned based on the value of the provided message. For example, of `pose` "
"is left empty, the pose of the entity will be set to the origin."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:179
msgid ""
"This might be resolved in the future. See https://github.com/ros-simulation/"
"simulation_interfaces/issues/18"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../ros2_sim_interfaces.md:183
msgid ""
"In Gazebo Harmonic, the twist of an entity is reset back to zero after each "
"time step. This is like applying a brake on the entity (see https://github."
"com/gazebosim/gz-sim/issues/1926). Thus, we do not recommend using "
"`SetEntityState` to control the twist. Later versions of Gazebo do not have "
"this problem. If you need to control the twist, consider using the "
"[VelocityControl](https://gazebosim.org/api/sim/8/"
"classgz_1_1sim_1_1systems_1_1VelocityControl.html) system."
msgstr ""

